Maruti Suzuki segments the Indian automobile market based on geographical, demographic, psychographic, and behavioral factors. Geographically, it segments based on country, urban vs rural areas. Demographically, its target audience is people over Rs. 400,000 annual income, those shifting from 2-wheelers to 4-wheelers aged 20-30. Psychographically, it offers differentiated products to attract all segments from economy to luxury cars. Behaviorally, it segments based on factors like power, technology, road warriors, generations, and price consciousness. Maruti Suzuki targets the broad Indian middle class market with its varied lineup.

