# Maruti Suzuki India: Market Analysis

Maruti Suzuki is a subsidiary of Suzuki Motor Corporation of Japan and has been the leader in the Indian car market for over two decades. It offers a wide range of affordable cars across segments. In 2010, Maruti Suzuki saw its highest ever sales of 1,271,005 vehicles, though net profits declined. It has a large sales and service network across India and exports have been increasing. Consumer behavior analysis shows that Indian customers prioritize affordable price, fuel efficiency, and low maintenance when choosing vehicles.

