# Maruti Suzuki inaugurates Kharkhoda plant in India

Kharkhoda's scale signals that India has moved from a protected domestic market to a cornerstone of Suzuki's global output strategy

 By  Automotive World

Maruti Suzuki India has inaugurated its Kharkhoda plant in Haryana, with Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Japanese counterpart Sanae Takaichi presiding via video link. The 800-acre facility is projected to cost INR 350bn (US$3.85bn) with an initial capacity of 500,000 units per year. [...] Let us help you understand the future of mobility

