- India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026: # India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026. **India’s passenger vehicle market reached a new high in January 2026, with 539,543 new registrations – the highest monthly total on record according to JATO Dynamics’ Retail Market Pulse report. This marks a 12.9% year-on-year growth from 477,764 units in January 2025, showing strong demand largely driven by retail buyers.**. “The automotive market in India has made a strong start this year, driven largely by strong nationwide retail demand, rising consumer aspirations, and wider model availability across segments. While the figures are based on retail registrations, institutional and bulk purchases also contribute to market volumes. Maruti Suzuki led the market with 229,456 registrations, up 6.7% year on year. Its market share slipped to 42.5%, down 2.48 percentage points year on year, as competition intensified across high-volume segments. Electric vehicles accounted for 4% of the market, with around 19,249 units registered, up from 15,288 units in December 2025.
