- How Maruti Cars Cater to the Needs of Indian Customers: # How Maruti Cars Cater to the Needs of Indian Customers. Maruti Suzuki has been a staple in the Indian automobile industry for several decades. It has consistently delivered on the evolving needs of Indian customers, offering a comfortable and safe driving experience on Indian roads. Maruti’s journey in the Indian market is a testament to its commitment to innovation, technology, and customer satisfaction. One of the key reasons why Maruti has been successful in India is its ability to understand the needs of its customers. Maruti’s customer-centric approach has helped the brand to create a range of cars that cater to the diverse needs of Indian customers. The brand has always been quick to respond to the changing needs of the market, introducing new models and features to stay ahead of the competition. Maruti has a deep understanding of the Indian market, and this has helped it to create cars that are perfectly suited to Indian conditions.
- Maruti Suzuki Stock 2026 | MSIL: India's Auto Giant, Growth Drivers ...: **The Thesis in One Line:** India’s biggest car maker is trading at a 20% discount to its historical average while volume growth is finally accelerating after two weak years, and the new SUV lineup is starting to pay off. This is the dominant player in India’s passenger vehicle market with a 41% market share. The business model is straightforward: manufacture vehicles at their plants in Haryana and Gujarat, sell them through 3,500+ dealerships across India, and earn additional revenue from spare parts and after-sales service. Here’s what matters: about 72% of revenue comes from compact and mid-size vehicles, 18% from utility vehicles (SUVs), and 10% from spare parts and services. Over the last three years, revenue grew at a 13.2% annual rate - that’s solid for a mature carmaker. Here’s what improved significantly: operating margins expanded from 9.8% in FY23 to 12.1% in FY24. The company’s also generating strong cash - operating cash flow per share hit ₹585 in FY24, up from ₹420 the previous year. [in C:\Users\Gaurav Srivastava\Desktop\dashify\api\routes\insights.py:234]
