Stagnant Income, Poor Infra, Maruti Suzuki Chairman Sounds Alarm Over Demand For Small Cars In India

Maruti Suzuki Chairman RC Bhargava sounded the alarm over demand for small cars in India, warning that car purchases in India are largely limited to the top 12% of households with an annual income exceeding ₹12 lakh, while even small cars have become unaffordable for the remaining 88%.

The statement comes during the post-results presser on April 25.

