- India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026: # India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026. **India’s passenger vehicle market reached a new high in January 2026, with 539,543 new registrations – the highest monthly total on record according to JATO Dynamics’ Retail Market Pulse report. This marks a 12.9% year-on-year growth from 477,764 units in January 2025, showing strong demand largely driven by retail buyers.**. “The automotive market in India has made a strong start this year, driven largely by strong nationwide retail demand, rising consumer aspirations, and wider model availability across segments. While the figures are based on retail registrations, institutional and bulk purchases also contribute to market volumes. Maruti Suzuki led the market with 229,456 registrations, up 6.7% year on year. Its market share slipped to 42.5%, down 2.48 percentage points year on year, as competition intensified across high-volume segments. Electric vehicles accounted for 4% of the market, with around 19,249 units registered, up from 15,288 units in December 2025.
- Maruti Suzuki Stock 2026 | MSIL: India's Auto Giant, Growth Drivers ...: **The Thesis in One Line:** India’s biggest car maker is trading at a 20% discount to its historical average while volume growth is finally accelerating after two weak years, and the new SUV lineup is starting to pay off. This is the dominant player in India’s passenger vehicle market with a 41% market share. The business model is straightforward: manufacture vehicles at their plants in Haryana and Gujarat, sell them through 3,500+ dealerships across India, and earn additional revenue from spare parts and after-sales service. Here’s what matters: about 72% of revenue comes from compact and mid-size vehicles, 18% from utility vehicles (SUVs), and 10% from spare parts and services. Over the last three years, revenue grew at a 13.2% annual rate - that’s solid for a mature carmaker. Here’s what improved significantly: operating margins expanded from 9.8% in FY23 to 12.1% in FY24. The company’s also generating strong cash - operating cash flow per share hit ₹585 in FY24, up from ₹420 the previous year. [in C:\Users\Gaurav Srivastava\Desktop\dashify\api\routes\insights.py:244]
