- Maruti Suzuki Car Sales February 2026 – Model-wise Analysis, YoY ...: # Maruti Suzuki Car Sales February 2026 – Model-wise Analysis, YoY & MoM Trends. Maruti Suzuki India Limited recorded domestic passenger vehicle sales of 1,61,000 units in February 2026, showing flat year-on-year growth compared to 1,60,791 units in February 2025. However, sales declined 8% month-on-month from 1,74,529 units in January 2026. Despite the flat overall performance, the model-wise breakdown reveals strong growth in sedans and MPVs, while entry-level hatchbacks and some SUVs experienced notable declines. This detailed analysis explores Maruti Suzuki's February 2026 sales trends, top-performing models, and key growth drivers. The standout performer in February was the Maruti Suzuki Dzire, which sold 19,326 units, registering a 32% year-on-year growth. The Dzire was Maruti Suzuki’s highest-selling car in February 2026. The Ertiga remains one of India’s most popular MPVs, while Brezza continues to dominate the compact SUV segment. The premium MPV Maruti Suzuki XL6 saw the highest growth across the portfolio, jumping 93% YoY to 3,633 units.
- India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026: # India's Passenger Vehicle Market Hits Record High in January 2026. **India’s passenger vehicle market reached a new high in January 2026, with 539,543 new registrations – the highest monthly total on record according to JATO Dynamics’ Retail Market Pulse report. This marks a 12.9% year-on-year growth from 477,764 units in January 2025, showing strong demand largely driven by retail buyers.**. “The automotive market in India has made a strong start this year, driven largely by strong nationwide retail demand, rising consumer aspirations, and wider model availability across segments. While the figures are based on retail registrations, institutional and bulk purchases also contribute to market volumes. Maruti Suzuki led the market with 229,456 registrations, up 6.7% year on year. Its market share slipped to 42.5%, down 2.48 percentage points year on year, as competition intensified across high-volume segments. Electric vehicles accounted for 4% of the market, with around 19,249 units registered, up from 15,288 units in December 2025. [in C:\Users\Gaurav Srivastava\Desktop\dashify\api\routes\insights.py:244]
