India's car market is back in top gear. Passenger vehicle sales jumped 28% in May 2026, with Maruti Suzuki, Tata Motors, Hyundai, Mahindra and Kia reporting strong growth. While SUVs continue to dominate, rising fuel costs are pushing more buyers towards CNG and EVs. Here's what the latest sales numbers reveal about changing consumer preferences and the future of India's auto market. Watch the video to know more.

